Ladybird applies the HTML element’s ASCII case folding to a named
property lookup on its attribute map. SVG and XML retain their case.
Blink’s NamedNodeMap::getNamedItem uses Element::getAttributeNode,
WebKit’s NamedNodeMap::isSupportedPropertyName uses
Element::hasAttribute, and Gecko’s nsDOMAttributeMap::NamedGetter looks
up the qualified name on the element.

Chrome 158.0.8127.37, Firefox 151.0, and WebKit 26.5 all returned
the attribute for a mixed-case property read. Firefox and WebKit also
recognized that spelling through the in operator and Object.hasOwn.
Chrome recognized only the lowercase spelling for those queries. None
included the mixed-case alias in its own property names.
